"""Documented hydropower crises tied to reservoirs in the watch list, with sources.

Fixed before scoring. Dates are the earliest date the cited source supports; when a source gives only
a month, the date is the 1st of that month and `date_precision` says so.

Scoring rule (set once, applied to every crisis, never tuned per crisis):
  * `reservoir_id` is the main storage reservoir behind the crisis (for multi-reservoir crises the
    largest-storage G-REALM lake of the affected system; the others are scored too, as `also`).
  * Our alarm = first monthly issue in the 12 months up to and including the onset month whose
    P(level below its same-month 20th percentile) exceeds 0.5 in any of the next 12 months.
  * Caught = that alarm was issued in a month before the onset month (lead >= 1 month).
  * `official_warning` = first public warning by a government, regulator or utility found; null if none found.
"""

